{"prompt": "We need a broad one-sentence world-model security claim with conceptual novelty 7-7.5. Current repository has official TD-MPC2 and MBRL-Lib/PETS, plus released WAV MiniGrid and WorldAgen. Existing screens rejected: action routing, terminal routing, temporal correlation, semigroup/order, CEM covariance, router/prototype hijack, branch observation splice, private queries, non-normal cascade as a broad mechanism, and generic TTT/cross-task interference.

Consider this materially different candidate: “A truthful action-only contributor can corrupt the *joint counterfactual coupling* of a shared world model without corrupting any individual action branch: each one-step branch marginal and on-policy forecast remains calibrated, but the set of branches no longer admits one shared latent physical mechanism. A planner that compares branches then selects a mutually incompatible trajectory, and the error persists after the contributor leaves.” The attack should use legal sequences that create overlapping intervention contexts, not edited outputs or sampling permutations. A matched control would preserve each branch marginal and action counts but preserve cross-branch coupling.

Assess whether this is genuinely distinct from WorldKernel, OneWorld, CoCo, ACID, generic counterfactual consistency, model error, and planner exploitation. If it can clear novelty 7, give an exact released carrier and two-minute gate using exact repository files/classes; if no carrier exists, reject. Be strict and do not recommend a long GPU run before a positive gate."}
